<title>SINGAPORE: SUTL, Tan&amp;Tan in Cambodia hotel JV -paper.</title>
<headline>SUTL, Tan&amp;Tan in Cambodia hotel JV -paper.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore property firm SUTL Corporation said it had signed up Malaysia's Tan &amp; Tan Development Bhd as its partner in a Singapore $35 million hotel project in Cambodia, said a report in Saturday's Straits Times.</p>
<p>SUTL leads a consortium of four companies and holds a 42 percent stake in the deal, with Tan &amp; Tan taking 40 percent.</p>
<p>The remaining 18 percent stake would be split evenly between fellow Singapore-based property firms Guthrie GTS Ltd and Lee Kim Tah Holdings Ltd. The project will develop a hotel complex with 172 apartments, sports, recreation, business and other facilities on a 70-year leasehold site in Phnom Penh, the report said.</p>
<p>Construction work on the site is due to begin in February and the complex is expected to be opened during 1998.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703011)</p>
